{"kind":"report","text":"Approved G0 exactfea7f73caac665f3a17935420c1e0ea45b5c3906, treed0a801da9841de8b405eefeed09e305bbc64a226, all3 artifacts with primary8e34e4ac first. Binding is ONLY isolated-object transport childb0140765/promise6c9ee717. P2 finding2dc3e4ae is resolved at this candidate. No remaining supported blocker found in this slice. Full e029 import bottleneck work, bounded path editor/queries/directory lifetime, G1 base-possession/publication and provider integration remain owed.\n\nArchitecture: isolation is explicit and fixed at source construction. Existing provider/default closure callers are unchanged; no production caller switches mode. The new path requires advertised shallow/filter and reachable permission for nonadvertised objects, requests deepen1/tree:0, accepts an empty or one-wanted-commit shallow phase, its flush, NAK and exactly one self-contained commit/tree/blob. It rejects tags/deltas/extra objects in isolation and retains their prior default decoding. Verified object facts are not closure/ancestry/known-base proof. Reader still verifies the expected type. Git's primary pack/filter/capability documentation supports this candidate negotiation, while actual host support stays unproved: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitprotocol-pack ; https://git-scm.com/docs/git-rev-list ; https://git-scm.com/docs/gitprotocol-capabilities .\n\nSecurity and bounded work: capability/format/origin/media/redirect checks remain; denial never becomes absence and there is no fallback or internal retry. Pack count and caller inflated-size checks precede inflater work. Wire, decoded/cache bytes and packet/object counts are bounded. The owned-payload model admits one operation with16*maxBytes beside existing cache and lifetime-issued output; concurrent calls fail before borrowing it. Output copies/ref strings are conservatively charged rather than presumed released. The16x model is a code-level payload reservation, not measured peak memory: engine/platform buffers, metadata, allocator/GC and higher-level source-pool admission still require their own evidence. No global capacity claim follows from this per-source slice.\n\nP2 repair: #isolated owns an independent timer and races caller completion against it. Expiry sets #abandoned, requests abort and retains #busy/deadline/reservation permanently; cleanup need not settle before the caller refuses. All object/ref/refs entry points reject terminal sources. A late fetch cancels its response without consuming its body; #timely after awaits/before cache mutation and in #output prevents late cache/output progress. The finally block cannot make abandoned capacity reusable. Pending cancellation may still exist internally: this bounds one abandoned operation per source and proves no physical draining. Default-mode cleanup behavior is not promoted into this isolated guarantee.\n\nWitnesses and controls: the local real git http-backend witness uses a labelled HTTP adapter stand-in. Four explicit reads transfer one pack object each and under5000response bytes together beside40commit history and a large unrelated sibling; root/tree/blob and empty shallow cases are covered. A default full read refuses the same fixture budget, so the test does not mislabel isolation as closure. Focused malformed/denied/budget/copy/concurrency cases exercise meaningful protocol boundaries. New fake-clock cases cover pending read and bad-status cleanup cancellation, then late fetch and late cleanup completion; caller settles at expiry, abort/cancel are requested, late body pulls stay zero and all3 entry points remain terminal with no additional fetch. My earlier independent standard-stream probe established the cancellation premise without importing project code.\n\nThe first pre-inflation control is bound to original88dd validator SHA2562a3882eef430958f3c431aa7e9c335a260987cf6c5351411846b91949ec482b9; it removes only the caller allowance guard. The corrected completion control removes only the outer race, preser